Falsifies `extensible_host_controller_interface::verification::a_producer_and_a_consumer_agree_across_the_wrap`.

The defect: the link TRB loses its Toggle Cycle bit, so the controller keeps its old cycle state past the wrap while the producer flips its own.

Expected to fail: the harness's check that the controller sees a TRB exactly when one is outstanding.

diff --git a/src/transfer_request_block.rs b/src/transfer_request_block.rs
--- a/src/transfer_request_block.rs
+++ b/src/transfer_request_block.rs
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@
     pub const fn link(target: u64) -> TransferRequestBlock {
         TransferRequestBlock::pointer(
             target,
-            [0, control(transfer_request_block_type::LINK) | 1 << 1],
+            [0, control(transfer_request_block_type::LINK)],
         )
     }
 
